Asya Takken wrote:
>
> Hi. I'm playing a neutral wizard character, currently in mine town,
> hanging out by the (co-aligned) altar.  I don't have any artifacts yet
> and could certainly do with Magicbane, nor do I have many intrinsics. 
> What should I do?  If I want an artifact, should I just keep
> sacrificing without praying in between?

There's only one weapon that can be given to a Neutral during
prayer and it isn't Magicbane.  For that matter Wizards get
(sometimes ore always I'm not positive) a spellbook of finger
of death rather than Vorpalblade so a Wizard might never get
a weapon from praying.

Sac for weapons, pray for other benefits.  Sac until you are
happy with your stock of weapons, pray until you are happy
with the other benefits you've gotten.

> Or should I pray whenever I get the "reconciliation" message?

This will guarantee you never get Magicbane.

> I bought protection from the priest once, and was only able to do that
> because I came across a Healer bones pile.  Is it worth trying to
> scrounge up the money to buy more?

Tastes vary.  Money is good in shops to buy items and in shrines
to buy protection.  Blow your cash on one and you get less of
the other.  Some want as much AC as possible as early as possible
while others prefer being able to buy stuff too heavy for their
pet to take.

> I'm already level 8, so it'd take me a while.  How do people get
> enough money to repeatedly buy protection, anyway?

Much deeper than you are now gold becomes more common.  Also if
you get the messages that there's a vault on the level, feel free
to dig until you find it.

> I do have one scroll of gold detection (and could
> probably write more but would rather save the marker for better
> scrolls).

Gold detection has an important use in the end game.  Consider
saving 4 of them.

> I don't think I want to kill any shopkeepers.

There are ways to extract their money and most of their items.

